# Next steps for {{ workspace_name }}

Your workspace is bootstrapped. The canonical PR flow walks from this empty
state through importing existing models, adding your own model, pulling
processes, capturing expert input, building a baseline, and implementing
phases of model extension. Each stage lands as its own PR.

Tick boxes as you go.

## Setup (now)

- [ ] `git init && git add -A && git commit -m "feat(stage-0): workspace bootstrap"`
- [ ] Create the venv: `uv venv .venv`
- [ ] **Activate it** in your shell: `source .venv/bin/activate`
      *(every new shell needs this; subsequent commands assume the venv is active)*
- [ ] Install workspace deps: `uv pip install -e ".[dev]"`
      *(if you skipped activation: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python -e ".[dev]"`)*
- [ ] Lint: `python scripts/lint-workspace.py` should print `workspace lint: OK`

> **Push to GitHub later.** It's tempting to `gh repo create` right now, but
> the canonical convention is to push *after* you've registered at least one
> model (Stage 1+2 below) — that way the first GitHub commit already shows
> the workspace doing something. See the **Publish** section after Stage 1+2.

## Stage 0.5 — Import existing models *(optional)*

If your project builds on an existing model (e.g., `vivarium-collective/v2ecoli`),
register it here. Three modes:

- **reference** — read-only submodule under `external/<name>/` for citation,
  comparison, or per-file cherry-pick.
- **fork-source** — catalog-only seed for a future `/pbg-add-model --from-import`
  (no checkout yet).
- **in-place** — submodule under `models/<name>/` with `external: true`; you
  operate against an external repo and PRs from this workspace open against
  the upstream remote.

Workflow:

- [ ] *(plugin path)* `/pbg-import-models <name> --source <url> --ref <ref> --mode <reference|fork-source|in-place>`
- [ ] *(no-plugin path)* edit `workspace.yaml.imports` directly + run
      `git submodule add <source> external/<name>` (or `models/<name>` for in-place mode)

Full lifecycle: `pbg-superpowers/skills/pbg-import-models/SKILL.md`.

## Stage 1+2 — Add a model

Each model lives under `models/<name>/` as a git submodule (its own GitHub repo).

- [ ] Scaffold from the model template (in `pbg-superpowers/templates/model/`) into a fresh sibling dir, e.g. `~/code/<name>/`
- [ ] In that dir: `git init && git add -A && git commit -m "feat(M3-stage-2): model package scaffold"`, then `gh repo create <org>/<name> --public --source=. --remote=origin --push`
- [ ] Back in the workspace: `git submodule add https://github.com/<org>/<name>.git models/<name>`
- [ ] Add the entry under `workspace.yaml.models.<name>` (`submodule_path`, `remote`, `pbg_processes: []`, `stages.add_model.status: complete`)
- [ ] `python scripts/lint-workspace.py` to confirm

Full lifecycle: `pbg-superpowers/skills/pbg-add-model/SKILL.md`.

## Publish — push the workspace to GitHub

Now that the workspace has at least one model + (optionally) imports, the
first GitHub commit shows real structure rather than an empty scaffold.

- [ ] Create the workspace repo on GitHub and push:
  ```
  gh repo create <org>/{{ workspace_name }} --public --source=. --remote=origin --push
  ```
- [ ] Make sure each model submodule's GitHub repo also exists (you should
      have done that during Stage 1+2 above).
- [ ] Collaborators clone with:
  ```
  git clone https://github.com/<org>/{{ workspace_name }}.git
  cd {{ workspace_name }}
  git submodule update --init --recursive
  ```

Workflow CI (`.github/workflows/workspace-ci.yml`) runs lint + per-model
pytest on every push.

## Stages 3 – 9..N — driving each stage

Each stage below has a shell script in `scripts/` that walks you through it
without requiring the `pbg-superpowers` plugin. Run from the workspace root.

### Stage 3 — pull processes *(plugin-only for now)*

Pull required `pbg-*` wrappers and register them in `models/<name>/pbg_<slug>/core.py`.
Use the plugin's `/pbg-pull-processes <model>` skill, or follow
`pbg-superpowers/skills/pbg-pull-processes/SKILL.md` manually.

### Stage 4 — datasets

- [ ] `bash scripts/add-dataset.sh`
      *(prompts: name, path/url, sha256 if url, claims served)*

### Stage 5 — references

- [ ] `bash scripts/add-reference.sh`
      *(paste a BibTeX entry; optionally map its key to claim IDs)*

### Stage 6 — expert input

- [ ] `bash scripts/add-acceptance.sh`
      *(captures one "if X, then Y" acceptance test for a model)*

### Stage 7 — baseline *(plugin-only for now)*

The baseline scaffolds a Composite from `pbg-composer`. Use the plugin's
`/pbg-baseline <model>` skill, or follow `pbg-superpowers/skills/pbg-baseline/SKILL.md`
manually.

### Stage 8 — phase plan

- [ ] `bash scripts/add-phase-plan.sh`
      *(prompts: model name, N phases, name + objective per phase. Writes
      `phases/plan.md` + `phases/phase-N.md` and updates workspace.yaml.)*

### Stages 9..N — phase implementation

- [ ] `bash scripts/start-phase.sh <model> <n>`
      *(opens phase n; refuses if phase n-1 hasn't passed its gate. Generates
      `tests/test_phases.py` placeholders from acceptance frontmatter.)*
- [ ] Implement each test body; update each `acceptance_tests[*].status` in
      the phase frontmatter as you go (`pending` → `passing` / `failing`).
- [ ] `bash scripts/evaluate-phase-gate.sh <model> <n>` to mark the phase
      complete when all acceptance tests pass.

These scripts call vendored copies of the `pbg-superpowers` Python helpers
(under `scripts/_lib/`) — same code path as the plugin, just runnable from
inside the workspace.

Full design: see `pbg-superpowers/docs/superpowers/specs/`.

## Two paths

- **With Claude Code + the [pbg-superpowers plugin](https://github.com/vivarium-collective/pbg-superpowers):**
  every stage above is a `/pbg-*` skill that walks the interactive flow and
  opens a clean PR.
- **Without the plugin:** use the `scripts/` shell scripts above for stages
  4–6, 8, 9..N. For stages 3 and 7, follow the relevant `SKILL.md` manually.
  Run `python scripts/lint-workspace.py` after every change.

## Config files to know

- `workspace.yaml` — canonical state (models registered, imports catalog, stage status per model)
- `docs/decisions.yaml` — append-only design log; every stage skill writes here
- `references/{papers.bib, claims.yaml}` — bibliography + claim → paper mapping
- `datasets/_index.yaml` — dataset registry
- `.pbg/schemas/` — workspace + phase JSON schemas (used by `lint-workspace.py`)

## When stuck

1. Run `python scripts/lint-workspace.py` — most workspace-shape issues surface here.
2. Open the relevant `SKILL.md` in `pbg-superpowers/skills/`.
3. File an issue at <https://github.com/vivarium-collective/pbg-superpowers/issues>.
